INT. HYPERBARIC CHAMBER - NIGHT

Steel hull. Porthole glass. Pipes that shudder as pressure climbs.

DR. NAOMI ESCOBEDO (40s, scrubs, calm eyes) adjusts a valve while PAUL ZIELINSKI (60s, diver, wrapped in a thin blanket) stares at the gauge and TECH ARDEN FLETCHER (20s, headset, ponytail) logs numbers on a clipboard beyond the porthole, tapping the glass whenever the needle moves.

CHARGE NURSE BIRGITTA (V.O.)
(intercom)
Chamber, status?

NAOMI
Two atmospheres. Holding.

PAUL
Twice the weight on my chest. Same as the day I surfaced too fast.

NAOMI
You came up in eleven minutes. Nobody does that and walks.

PAUL
I walked.

NAOMI
You crawled. I read the report.

PAUL
I don't remember crawling.

NAOMI
You will tomorrow.

PAUL
Will I.

NAOMI
That's what we do here.

BIRGITTA (V.O.)
(intercom)
Doctor, ten minutes remaining.

NAOMI
Copy.
